  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DescriptionOfTheRiskOrConcern' (DescriptionOfTheRiskOrConcern) is 'LCA exercise has not revealed any specific risks or concerns across the 5 relevant impact categories, namely Acidification, Global Warming, Marine Eutrophication, Freshwater Eutrophication and Water Scarcity.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DescriptionOfTheRiskOrConcern, Context: D_ProductOrService1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'ActionTaken' (ActionTaken) is 'RIL has set an ambitious goal to achieve Net Carbon Zero by 2035 and continues to advance steadily on its energy transition pathway. The Company is developing a fully integrated renewable energy ecosystem - anchored by giga-scale manufacturing of solar PV modules, energy storage systems and electrolysers - to establish and enable 100 GW renewable energy by 2030 and to support green hydrogen production with a plan to scale up to 3 MMTPA of green hydrogen equivalent production capacity by 2032. During FY 2025–26, focused efforts were undertaken to strengthen its New Energy ecosystem, increase renewable energy uptake, expand bioenergy integration and enhance process efficiencies across operations. These initiatives are aimed at ensuring secure, reliable and cost-effective clean energy for captive consumption.\n\nAt the same time, RIL remains committed to lowering the energy intensity of its own operations through energy efficient project design for new projects and continued process optimisation. Together, these measures are expected to further reduce greenhouse gas emissions and mitigate acidification impacts across its value chain.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: ActionTaken, Context: D_ProductOrService1)"
  },
